  "challenge": "The packet already supports a clean REJECT rather than ESCALATE. QuickShip is absent from master (VN-001), the claimed predecessor FastShip Ltd. is INACTIVE with zero invoices and zero paid history, and the invoice itself carries no address or email—so there is no live relationship, payment trail, or contact channel left to 'verify with procurement.' Policy treats unknown vendor as the primary fraud entry point and flags an inactive-successor claim as the VN-004 signal; stacking that with a $9,975 total sitting inside the PO-002 near-threshold band is enough to refuse payment until the vendor is formally onboarded or reactivated through the ordinary channel. Escalation only delays the same outcome: nothing in the prior-tool results can turn an unregistered, uncontactable name with a dormant claim into a payable vendor.",
  "proposed_outcome": "REJECT",
  "cites_finding_codes": ["VN-001", "VN-004", "PO-002"]
}
